OL,3,GNEWSASwinney to cut number of health
OL,4,Aboards from 14 to two
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first minister has confirmed plans
OL,7,Fto cut the number of health boards
OL,8,Fproviding local services across
OL,9,FScotland from 14 to two.
OL,11,FExisting boards could be merged so that
OL,12,Fthere would be one for the west and
OL,13,Fanother for the east of Scotland.
OL,15,FSeparate plans are being considered for
OL,16,Fthe three island groups - Shetland,
OL,17,FOrkney, and the Western Isles.
OL,19,FSetting out his programme for
OL,20,Fgovernment, Swinney called the move
OL,21,F"the most significant structural reform
OL,22,Fof our NHS in the devolution era".
